## 2. Tea Line Four Loses the Snare During Reseal

**Story & Context:** At 124 BPM, Mara programs the EP's most rigid industrial rhythm, with compact kick, metallic backbeat, and narrow relay-click pattern. Nino plays a three-note chiboni cell across long pressure cycles. Every RESEAL phase is given a different electronic vacancy: first the snare disappears, then the sub, then the entire upper percussion layer. Tamar answers each vacancy with one clipped Pianet fifth. Giorgi uses doli only where the programmed snare is absent. Leonie contributes short breath-led bass-clarinet notes in the gaps between sub entries. The central break removes all machine percussion for one full pressure cycle, leaving bagpipe, Pianet, and doli to prove that the Bellows Relay remains legible without the industrial chassis.

